CORE gcc-only
main_msvc.c
-D_MSC_VER=1950 --pointer-check
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.[0-9]+\] line 18 memcpy source region readable: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of [0-9]+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The library models of memcpy and memmove follow the Microsoft runtime when
preprocessed by cl (_MSC_VER): a null pointer with a zero length is not an
error. Only the copy with a non-zero length from a null pointer fails.
gcc-only: cl defines _MSC_VER itself.
